Template for projects/<project>/<harness>/Characterise.v: the classifier
templates.  These are not claims; each is a property of a program C that a
prover supplies.

@@ file
(** * $project / $harness: characterisation problems

$header *)

From Stdlib Require Import QArith.
From LinuxProcessSemantics.LinuxProcessSem Require Import MemImageType.
From $namespace.Core Require Import Shapes.
From $rocq Require Images$distribution_require.
$definitions
@@ header
These are not claims.  Each is a property of a classifier program [C], which is any static riscv64 Linux executable you supply$and_bound.  A result is a [C] with a proof of [<build>_classifies C]$and_rejects.  Together with [image_wf C] such a result proves [Statements.<build>_agreement_decidable]$and_claim.

@@ and_bound
, and of a bound [b]
@@ and_rejects
 and of [<build>_classifier_rejects_at_most C b] for as small a [b] as you can
@@ and_claim
, and (through [Shapes.disagrees_at_most_of_classifier]) [Statements.<build>_disagrees_at_most b]

@@ definition
(** $doc *)
Definition $name$params : Prop :=
  $body.

@@ doc_classifies
[C] exits 0 exactly on the finite inputs where the plain and $san builds agree, and 1 on the others.
@@ doc_rejects
Under [Distribution.w], the inputs [C] rejects weigh at most [b].
